            "review_title": "Review at Happy Lamb Hot Pot Vietnam",
            "review_text": "Kiwidundee\nThames, New Zealand119 contributions\n0\nLoved the experience\nAug 2024 • Couples\nWe saw this restaurant walking past from our hotel and because there were a lot of people inside we decided to have dinner there. Its a traditional hot pot, but they specialise in lamb, and, being from New Zealand, this suited us fine. When the food appeared at the table, along with the pho broth for cooking it, I didn't think we would finish it, but it was beautiful, yummy and healthy. There were heaps of greens, three different mushroom types, two different pho (one \"mild\" and one tomato based), and strips of lamb and beef. All of it goes into the hot pot in the centre of the table, with some ramen noodles. There was a special on drinks as well, so we took advantage of that. All in all a great experience and obviously popular with the locals.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nAsk staff if you are not sure of the menu, and they will only be too happy to provide some recommendations.\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten August 18, 2024",
